    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "Yes, 89-9. And welcome back. You're tuning in to the HRSA Nation Video Show, and I'm your host, Anthony Ray. And we're so blessed today to be joined in the broadcast with the chairman of the Congressional Black Caucus, Congressman G. K. Butterfield. Congressman Butterfield graduated from college and law school at North Carolina Central University in HBCU. And then Congress Butterfield is the champion of affordable health care education, investments in rural communities, veterans, renewable energies, and federal programs that support low-income and middle-class Americans. Butterfield serves in the Democratic leadership as Chief Deputy Whip and Chair of the Congressional Black Caucus. He sits on the influential Committee on Energy and Commerce as the fifth-most senior Democrat on the Health Subcommittee. Congressman Butterfield, welcome back to the show. Well, thank you. It's good to be with you again. Mr. Chairman, you suggested in a speech on Capitol Hill in the aftermath of the death of Freddie Gray in Baltimore that unrest in urban areas connected to police involved fatalities of unarmed blacks is also related to economic disparity. And in an op-ed piece, you pin together with Representative Carolyn Maloney. You say it's time to face truth about poverty in America. Mr. Chairman, is Black America in a state of emergency?",
