    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "the reason is because Black America is in a state of emergency. One only needs to look at the statistics to get a full understanding of where we are as a community. One out of four African-American families lives in poverty. That's 25%. One out of three African-American children live in poverty. And so by anyone's definition, we are in a crisis and it is indeed a state of emergency. If you would look at the employment statistics, you will come to the same conclusion. You'd look at the income disparity and wealth disparity and the poverty rates in the various communities. You will see that we are indeed an across crisis. When you look at housing statistics and educational attainment, all of these data point to one inescapable conclusion. And that is this is an emergency. And those of us who serve an elective office and those of us in policy making positions, we've got to become proactive and we've got to make the case.",
