    "turn_idx": 16,
    "turn_text": "we've got to educate the public about the crisis that we are facing. I believe that there are some opportunities to enter into some type of bipartisan legislation with Republicans. There are not many, but I believe that particularly in the area of criminal justice reform, there may be some appetite on the part of some Republican to legislate in that direction. But we've got to clean up many of these police departments across the country that are just out of control. And the US Justice Department knows that they're out of control. And anyone who lives in black neighborhoods, in urban America and rural America, we all know that police misconduct is an everyday episode in too many communities. And so we've got to come up with legislation that will discourage and provide disincentive uh... for police officers to do what they did to michael brown and and credit gray and others who have fallen for the twenty african-americans have been senselessly and needlessly and unlawfully killed over the last two years. And that must stop.",
